# component: toast
# decisions: A11Y-3, A11Y-4, A11Y-8, A11Y-9, COL-12, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, OVL-13
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: the toast root's `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring
#     focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:ring-ring/50` halo goes; dropping `outline-none` lets
#     the single 2px `:focus-visible` outline `base.css` owns through.
#   COL-12: `ToastIcon` paints each type in its own status family — `success`, `info` and
#     `warning` gain an ink where upstream left them inheriting the body colour, and `error`
#     moves from the `destructive` FILL to `destructive-text`. The `-text` role is the one that
#     passes AA as ink on a `popover` surface, which is the pair A11Y-13 named in Batch 2.
#   A11Y-9: `tabIndex` follows `aria-hidden`. For a `priority: "high"` toast,
#     `@base-ui/react@1.8.0` (`toast/root/ToastRoot.js`, the `isHighPriority` block) announces a
#     visually hidden `role="alert"` clone in the viewport and marks the VISIBLE root
#     `role="alertdialog" aria-hidden="true"` for as long as the viewport is unfocused, so the
#     polite region does not announce it twice — while leaving `tabIndex: 0` on the root and on
#     its action and close buttons. Nothing tabbable may sit inside an `aria-hidden` subtree, so
#     a keyboard user tabs onto a control no screen reader will name (axe: SERIOUS
#     `aria-hidden-focus`). A11Y-9 is that invariant — what is hidden from assistive technology
#     must not be reachable by keyboard — stated for the modal surfaces; this is the same
#     invariant on a non-modal one, so it is implemented under the existing row rather than a new
#     one. The root's `render` reads `aria-hidden` OFF THE PROPS BASE UI HANDS IT, rather than
#     recomputing `priority === "high" && !focused`, so the hunk keeps matching if upstream
#     changes the condition; it publishes the flag on `ToastHiddenFromAtContext`, and `ToastAction`
#     and `ToastClose` — the focusable parts this file owns — mirror it. `inert` is deliberately
#     NOT used: it would also kill the mouse, and an unfocused error toast's Retry button has to
#     stay clickable. Base UI clears `aria-hidden` the moment the viewport takes focus (F6), so the
#     toast re-enters the tab order exactly when it becomes visible to assistive technology;
#     `toast.test.tsx` walks that round trip and audits the high-priority state with NO axe
#     suppression list, pinning the engine's shape beside it so the hunk fails as stale the day
#     Base UI fixes this. Worth reporting to Base UI.
#   OVL-13: `ToastPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class.
#   A11Y-8: NO HUNK. Upstream already signals type with a shape as well as a colour — `ToastIcon`
#     renders a distinct lucide glyph per type, and the COL-12 hunk above only colours glyphs that
#     are already there. `toast.test.tsx` asserts the icon, so a future upstream that drops it
#     fails here.
#   A11Y-3, A11Y-4: NO HUNK. Base UI's `Toast.Viewport` IS the mounted-for-life polite region this
#     policy asks for — `role="region"`, `aria-live="polite"`, rendered by `Toaster` whether or
#     not a toast exists — and per-toast urgency is the manager's `priority: "high"`. Adding a
#     second region would announce every toast twice. `toast.test.tsx` asserts the region's shape.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
